# crypto-bigint 0.7.6, RustCrypto/crypto-bigint c34044b8a1479ef32bec0a9030cf2f07b06506d9.
# Package SHA256: 6bb08299a6046833a879ace115697f12fd2bd6c8d3e93c909ffc9e0738e7cae0.
# Upstream sources and Apache-2.0/MIT notices are retained. Cargo.toml declares
# the mixed license; LICENSE-AGPL is added. Cargo cache metadata and lock omitted.
#
# Uint::borrowing_sub keeps ctutils::Choice for 17-word, 32-bit integers only.
# This is P-521's integer width; other widths retain the upstream word loop.
# Each word still uses the original protected subtraction primitive. Only the
# intermediate Choice-to-mask-to-Choice round trips are removed. Initial MSB
# interpretation and the final protected full mask are unchanged; the upstream
# zero-width path returns the original arbitrary borrow without normalizing it.
# No change to Limb, UintRef, BoxedUint, division or safegcd implementations.
# crypto-bigint 0.7.6 and ctutils 0.4.5 security fixes remain in place.
#
# crates/rsk-ec/tests/uint_borrow.rs compares this method with independent
# two's-complement addition, including dense chains, boundaries and const use.
# The same test can run against the actual 32-bit backend with cpubits="32"
# in an isolated package; that checks arithmetic, not ARM code generation.
#
